-- title:
--   Coefficientwise p-integrality of p⁻¹wₚ t_l
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $r$ a natural number, and let $D$ be a `FamData p r`, that is: a family $t : \mathrm{Fin}\,r \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-modular function field of level $1\cdot p$, a family $t^{\mathrm{Rat}}$ of elements of `modularFunctionFieldFull (1 * p)` (the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}$-Laurent series generated by the $q$-expansions $q\mapsto j(q^d)$ for $d \mid 1\cdot p$), and the requirement that each $t_l$ is the image of $t^{\mathrm{Rat}}_l$ under coefficientwise extension of scalars along $\mathbb{Q}\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Assume: (i) `hbasis`, that $(t_l)$ is linearly independent over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and spans the Riemann–Roch space of the divisor $\mathrm{embDegree}(1\cdot p)\cdot[\bar\infty]$, i.e. the functions whose polar behaviour is bounded by that divisor; (ii) `horthZero`, that for every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,r\to\mathbb{Q}$ all Laurent coefficients of $\sum_i c_i\,w_p(t^{\mathrm{Rat}}_i)$ have non-negative $p$-adic valuation if and only if $v_p(c_i)\ge -\mathrm{hasseExp}(D,i)$ for every $i$, where $w_p$ is `frickeInvolutionFull (1 * p)` and $\mathrm{hasseExp}(D,i)$ is the non-negative part of the least $p$-adic valuation of a non-zero coefficient of the associated zero-series; (iii) `hge1`, that $\mathrm{hasseExp}(D,l)\ge 1$ for every index $l\ge 1$. Then for every index $l\ge 1$ and every $m\in\mathbb{Z}$, the rational number $p^{-1}$ times the $m$-th Laurent coefficient of $w_p(t^{\mathrm{Rat}}_l)$ has non-negative $p$-adic valuation.
--
--   This records the $p$-integrality of $p^{-1}w_p t_l$ coefficient by coefficient for all members of the family away from the index $0$: since the content of $w_p t_l$ is at least $1$, every coefficient of $w_p t_l$ is divisible by $p$ (the statement is phrased so that vanishing coefficients cause no trouble). It supplies the cusp-$0$ side hypothesis used in the construction of a good family on the $\bar\infty$-chart, and is cited by [`ModularCurve.MultCovering.exists_famCtx`](thm.html#ModularCurve.MultCovering.exists_famCtx) and [`ModularCurve.MultCovering.exists_famCtx_orth_linearIndependent_zeroChart_residue`](thm.html#ModularCurve.MultCovering.exists_famCtx_orth_linearIndependent_zeroChart_residue).
